            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.088,
            0.526,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "metal oxides and minerals, and in the air as carbon dioxide. While discussing the oxygen cycle, we focus on processes that regulate the oxygen level in the atmosphere (Fig. 13.16). Organisms like plants and animals use oxygen for respiration, and releases "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { { C O } _ { 2 ^ { \\circ } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Combustion of fuels uses oxygen and releases "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { { C O } _ { 2 ^ { \\circ } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Plants restore oxygen through photosynthesis using sunlight, water and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to form glucose and release "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { O } _ { 2 ^ { \\bullet } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " This balance between consumption (respiration and combustion) and production (photosynthesis) circulates oxygen between the atmosphere, land, oceans and living organisms, sustaining life across all spheres of the Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
